\section{Compensation Training Convergence}
\label{app:comp_convergence}

All compensation networks~\cite{gautam2026fastforward} were trained for 1000 steps (lr=$10^{-4}$, batch size 4, seq length 2048). Training loss plateaus by step 700 across all valid runs: 30\% s42 (final loss 0.70), 30\% s456 (0.68), 50\% s42 (1.07), with $<$5\% variation over the final 300 steps. The compensation network converges but provides no quality improvement over the KL predictor alone, confirming that the redundancy result reflects predictor self-sufficiency rather than insufficient compensation training. % exp_id: kl_comp_30_s42, kl_comp_30_s456, kl_comp_50_s42

